WEBVTT

00:00:00.687 --> 00:00:06.038
This is FlightDeck. It runs your AI coding agents side by side:

00:00:06.038 --> 00:00:10.625
here on devbox, a worker machine, driven from the Mac.

00:00:10.916 --> 00:00:13.810
Start an agent, and tell it what to build.

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:17.186
Every agent gets its own git branch and worktree.

00:00:26.156 --> 00:00:29.128
Then start another, while the first one works.

00:00:41.664 --> 00:00:45.426
Mission control shows every agent at once, as live tiles.

00:00:49.235 --> 00:00:52.340
When an agent needs you, it comes first.

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:54.436
Answer right from its tile.

00:01:01.242 --> 00:01:07.604
Both are done. Try a change in the session's own browser, where localhost is the worker.

00:01:20.824 --> 00:01:26.257
Happy with it? Finish merges the branch into main, and cleans up the worktree.

00:01:27.666 --> 00:01:33.456
That's FlightDeck: many agents, one window, and you stay in control.

00:01:33.456 --> 00:01:36.861
The tutorials show every step in detail.
